<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A panel that slides in from a screen edge, with swipe-to-dismiss and snap points.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/drawer)

<%= embed AppicaUI::DrawerPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Drawer(side: :right) do
  DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Open drawer" } }
  DrawerContent do
    DrawerHeader do
      DrawerTitle { "Notifications" }
      DrawerDescription { "Choose what you want to be notified about." }
    end
    DrawerBody { ... }
    DrawerFooter do
      DrawerClose { |close| Button(**close) { "Save" } }
      DrawerClose { |close| Button(**close, variant: :outline) { "Cancel" } }
    end
  end
end
```

Drawer is a compound component built on a native `<dialog>`. Pick the edge with `side:`; the
swipe direction follows it automatically. By default it's modal and dismissible, with a drag
handle and a corner close button:

- **DrawerTrigger** - the button that opens the drawer. A block with an argument receives the
  trigger attributes, so you can render your own Button.
- **DrawerContent** - the panel. It draws the card, backdrop, handle and corner close button.
  Opened with `showModal()`, it sits in the top layer, so it needs no portal.
- **DrawerHeader** - groups the title and description with consistent spacing.
- **DrawerTitle** - an `<h2>` that labels the panel (`aria-labelledby`).
- **DrawerDescription** - a `<p>` that describes it (`aria-describedby`).
- **DrawerBody** - the main content region; it owns the scroll.
- **DrawerFooter** - the actions, stacked at the bottom of the panel.
- **DrawerClose** - a button that dismisses the drawer; same block convention as the trigger.

Reach for a Drawer when the surface should feel anchored to an edge or be swipeable on touch -
navigation, filters, a detail panel, a mobile sheet.

## Examples

### Sides

Set `side:` to `:top`, `:right`, `:bottom`, or `:left`. Left and right read as side panels; top
and bottom as sheets - cap the sheet's width (`class: "mx-auto max-w-2xl"` on `DrawerContent`)
so it doesn't stretch edge-to-edge on a wide screen.

<%= embed AppicaUI::DrawerPreview, :sides %>

```ruby
Drawer(side: :bottom) do
  DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Bottom" } }
  DrawerContent(class: "mx-auto max-w-2xl") { ... }
end
```

### Snap points & scrollable content

`snap_points:` lets a top or bottom drawer rest at intermediate heights. Each value is a fraction
of the viewport (0-1), a pixel number (> 1), or a CSS length string (`"24rem"`). The drawer opens
at the first point; drag or flick between them, and it dismisses past the smallest.

For content taller than the panel, let `DrawerBody` own the overflow between a pinned header and
footer. A left/right drawer is the natural fit: its swipe is horizontal, so it never fights the
vertical scroll.

<%= embed AppicaUI::DrawerPreview, :long_content %>

```ruby
Drawer(snap_points: [ 0.4, 1 ]) do
  DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Open player" } }
  DrawerContent(class: "mx-auto max-w-2xl") { ... }
end
```

### Nested drawers

A drawer can open another drawer: nest the markup inside `DrawerBody`. The parent tucks back as
the child slides in, and the child renders without a backdrop, as a solid card.

<%= embed AppicaUI::DrawerPreview, :nested %>

```ruby
Drawer(side: :right) do
  DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Workspace" } }
  DrawerContent do
    DrawerBody do
      Drawer(side: :right) do
        DrawerTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger) { "Rename workspace" } }
        DrawerContent(close_button: false) { ... }
      end
    end
  end
end
```

### Listening for changes

The controller dispatches `appica-ui--drawer:open-change` with `{ open }` and, for sheets with snap
points, `appica-ui--drawer:snap-point-change` with `{ snapPoint }`.

```ruby
Drawer(data: { action: "appica-ui--drawer:open-change->player#toggle" }) { ... }
```

### RTL

The header, body and footer read right-to-left and the handle and close button mirror. When RTL
is scoped to part of an LTR page, set `dir: "rtl"` on `DrawerContent` too.

<%= embed AppicaUI::DrawerPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Drawer

The root. Holds the edge and options and renders the Stimulus wrapper (`display: contents`).

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `side:` | `:top`, `:right`, `:bottom`, `:left` | `:bottom` | The edge the drawer slides in from. |
| `default_open:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Open on page load. |
| `modal:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Make the page inert and lock scroll while open. |
| `disable_pointer_dismissal:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Keep the drawer open when the backdrop is clicked. |
| `snap_points:` | `Array` | - | Resting heights for a top/bottom drawer (fraction, px, or CSS length). |
| `id:`, `data:`, … | | | Any other HTML attributes go on the root element. |

### DrawerTrigger / DrawerClose

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| block | `{ \|attributes\| … }` or `{ … }` | - | With an argument, yields the attributes to put on your own element; without one renders a plain `<button>`. |
| `class:`, … | | | Extra attributes merged into the yielded ones. |

### DrawerContent

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `close_button:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Render the × button in the corner. |
| `close_label:` | `String` | `"Close"` | Accessible label for the close button. |
| `backdrop:` | `Boolean` | top level: `true`, nested: `false` | Render the dimmed backdrop. |
| `frame:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Translucent glass frame around the panel. Needs the backdrop; without one the panel is a solid card. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes on the panel (e.g. `mx-auto max-w-2xl`). |

### DrawerHeader, DrawerTitle, DrawerDescription, DrawerBody, DrawerFooter

Layout parts. All accept `class:` (merged via tailwind_merge) and other HTML attributes.

## Accessibility

- The panel is a `<dialog>` opened with `showModal()`, with `aria-labelledby` / `aria-describedby`
  wired to `DrawerTitle` and `DrawerDescription` - always render a title.
- Opening moves focus into the panel and makes the rest of the page inert. Escape, a backdrop
  click, or a swipe toward the edge close it, and focus returns to the trigger.
- With `modal: true` (the default) page scroll is locked while the drawer is open.
- The corner close button carries an accessible label (`close_label:`).
- Enter/exit animations are skipped when the user prefers reduced motion.
